{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.SaturationRhoCap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SaturationRhoCap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.saturation_rho_cap_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.saturation_rho_cap_four","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SaturationRhoCap.lean#L44-L62","doc":"**A=4 saturation cap** (log-free): `det₄ = (1+3m)(1−m)³ ≥ (1−m²)⁶`,\nequivalently `ρ₄ ≤ 6`.  The ⁴He strong target `ρ_strong(4) ≈ 13` exceeds\nthis cap of `6`, so the isospin-even cumulant cannot supply the ⁴He\nbinding magnitude for any `m`.  The gap factorises as\n`m³(1−m)³·h(m)` with `h(m) = 8 + 6m − 6m² − 8m³ + 3m⁵ + m⁶`, and\n`h(m) = 8(1−m) + 6(m−m²) + 8(m−m³) + 3m⁵ + m⁶ ≥ 0` on `[0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.saturation_rho_cap_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.saturation_rho_cap_three","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SaturationRhoCap.lean#L33-L42","doc":"**A=3 saturation cap** (log-free): `det₃ = (1+2m)(1−m)² ≥ (1−m²)³`,\nequivalently `ρ₃ ≤ 3`.  The exact factorisation\n`(1+2m)(1−m)² − (1−m²)³ = m³(1−m)²(2+m)` exhibits the gap as a product of\nnon-negative factors on `[0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}